---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import HomeSections from '../components/HomeSections.astro';
import config from '../../site.config';
import { homeFaqs } from '../lib/home';
import { courseSchema, eventListingItem, faqSchema } from '../lib/schema';
import { absoluteUrl, getEventsForProgramme, getHomeUpcoming, getProgrammes, paths } from '../lib/site';
import { ogPathFor } from '../lib/og';

/*
 * The homepage publishes the cohorts it shows, machine-readably.
 *
 * Its graph was Organization, WebSite, WebPage and FAQPage - no event data at
 * all - while the second section of the page, directly under the hero, is the
 * dated "Next in Oxford" list, the hero's own button reads "Book the next
 * cohort", and the header and footer of all 63 pages name the next date. The
 * one page carrying the booking promise said nothing a machine could read
 * about what is being booked.
 *
 * This was backlog 40, and it waited two cycles for its own test: re-probe
 * once `/events/` had been recrawled, because if the same structured data did
 * nothing there it would do nothing here. Today's probes answered it from the
 * other direction. Restricting a search to this domain returns the SAME three
 * URLs whatever is asked - `/`, `/guides/claude-cowork-claude-code-or-codex/`
 * and `/guides/after-the-ai-executive-programme/` - and every event fact the
 * engine quoted, for both November cohorts and for the Coding Bootcamp, it
 * took off the homepage. `/events/` is not in that index, which is why its fix
 * could not move anything. The homepage is. So the structured data belongs
 * where a page is actually held.
 *
 * It is also where the reading went wrong: asked for the bootcamp, the engine
 * called the passed 21 October Second Brain day at the Pitt Rivers Museum "the
 * next listed cohort" and attributed it to the Agentic Bootcamp. A dated
 * `EducationEvent` per cohort, with its own `eventStatus`, is the thing that
 * contradicts that; prose alone could not.
 *
 * Nothing new is asserted. Each node is `eventListingItem`, under the same
 * `@id` the cohort's own page publishes, so a consumer holding both describes
 * one event rather than two, and it is the same set the cards below render -
 * from the same helper, so the markup cannot come to describe a cohort the
 * page does not show. `/home-photos/` deliberately does not get these: it is
 * noindex, and a page not offered to crawlers as an entity should not publish
 * entities.
 */
const upcoming = await getHomeUpcoming();
const eventNodes = upcoming.map((event) =>
  eventListingItem(event, absoluteUrl(ogPathFor(paths.event(event.data.slug)))),
);

/*
 * And the programmes it shows, for the same reason one cycle on.
 *
 * "What we run" renders a card per programme - name, pitch and a link - and
 * the graph said nothing about any of them, while three rich `Course` nodes
 * sat on `/bootcamps/<slug>/`, which no probe has ever returned. Today's
 * brand-and-month query is what makes this worth a cycle: asked for a
 * November cohort of this bootcamp, the engine answered off two expired Luma
 * pages, found no November date, and offered Oxford Saïd's four-week online
 * programme as a "possible mix-up". One day, in person, in Oxford, on a dated
 * instance is precisely what separates the two, and `courseMode`,
 * `courseWorkload` and `hasCourseInstance` say it in the form an engine reads.
 *
 * Every programme, not the three cohorts: the section shows all of them, and a
 * programme between cohorts is still a real course - it just publishes no
 * instance, which is honest about there being nothing to book. Each node comes
 * from the same helper the programme page uses, under that page's own `@id`,
 * so the two cannot come to disagree.
 */
const courseNodes = await Promise.all(
  (await getProgrammes()).map(async (programme) =>
    courseSchema(programme, (await getEventsForProgramme(programme.id)).upcoming),
  ),
);
---

{/* HomeSections already ends on the gold "Not ready to book?" band, which
    renders the same NewsletterForm with the same label and, with no
    newsletter endpoint set, the same fallback sentence. Two identical asks a
    screen apart read as a template fault rather than a second chance, so the
    footer's copy stands down here (footerSignup={false}). */}
<Base
  pageTitle={config.brand.tagline}
  titleOverride={`${config.brand.name} - ${config.brand.tagline}`}
  description={config.brand.description}
  path="/"
  ogImage={ogPathFor('/')}
  schemaNodes={[faqSchema(homeFaqs, '/'), ...eventNodes, ...courseNodes]}
  footerSignup={false}
>
  {/* Drummond's call (28 Jul): the homepage is the typographic design — ink,
      motif and micro-interactions. The photo variant lives at /home-photos/;
      swap the two withPhotos values to trade them back. */}
  <HomeSections withPhotos={false} />
</Base>
